        <briefdescription>
<para>This hook must be implemented to lower the incoming (formal) arguments, described by <computeroutput>VRegs</computeroutput>, for GlobalISel. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each argument must end up in the related virtual registers described by <computeroutput>VRegs</computeroutput>. In other words, the first argument should end up in <computeroutput>VRegs</computeroutput>[0], the second in <computeroutput>VRegs</computeroutput>[1], and so on. For each argument, there will be one register for each non-aggregate type, as returned by <computeroutput>computeValueLLTs</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>MIRBuilder</computeroutput> is set to the proper insertion for the argument lowering. <computeroutput>FLI</computeroutput> is required for sret demotion.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>True if the lowering succeeded, false otherwise. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
